# gcloud CLI access (KEM LLC)

## Install (macOS)

```bash
brew install --cask google-cloud-sdk
npm install -g firebase-tools
export PATH="/opt/homebrew/bin:$PATH"
```

## Login (required once per machine)

**Browser opens automatically:**
```bash
gcloud auth login
firebase login
```

**Headless / remote (Cursor agent or SSH):**
```bash
gcloud auth login --no-launch-browser
```
1. Open the printed Google URL in your browser.
2. Copy the **one-time verification code** (not a password — do not commit it).
3. Paste it into the terminal when prompted.

OAuth verification codes expire quickly and are **never** stored in `.env`. They complete CLI login only.

## Verify session

```bash
gcloud auth list
gcloud config get-value project
gcloud projects list
```

## Default project

```bash
gcloud config set project kem-llc-web
```

Override for scripts: `GCP_PROJECT_ID=your-project-id ./scripts/setup-gcp-auth.sh`

## Run KEM GCP setup

```bash
cd "/Users/rknptl/Desktop/kem llc website "
./scripts/setup-gcp-auth.sh
```

## Firebase CLI via gcloud (no `firebase login` needed)

```bash
./scripts/firebase-gcp.sh status
./scripts/firebase-gcp.sh deploy-rules
```

Uses `gcloud auth print-access-token` + vars in `.env.local`.

## Firebase MCP (Cursor)

Project MCP config: `.cursor/mcp.json` → runs `scripts/firebase-mcp.sh`.

Auth is automatic via **Application Default Credentials** (`~/.config/gcloud/application_default_credentials.json`). One-time setup:

```bash
./scripts/firebase-auth-setup.sh
# or: gcloud auth application-default login
```

Optional fallback: `firebase login:ci --no-localhost` → add `FIREBASE_TOKEN=...` to `.env.local` (never commit).

Reload Cursor after MCP config changes.

Useful MCP tools: `firebase_get_environment`, `firebase_get_sdk_config`, `firebase_get_security_rules`, `firebase_deploy`.


| Variable | File | Purpose |
|----------|------|---------|
| `VITE_FIREBASE_*` | `.env.local` / Vercel | Firebase client config (public keys) |
| `GCP_PROJECT_ID`, `GCP_PROJECT_NUMBER` | `.env.local` | Scripts + API calls |
| `FIREBASE_WEB_APP_ID` | `.env.local` | Firebase web app reference |
| `FIREBASE_TOKEN` | `.env.local` optional | Only from `firebase login:ci` — rarely needed |
| OAuth verification code | **Never** | One-time; paste at CLI prompt only |

## Troubleshooting

- `No credentialed accounts` → run `gcloud auth login` again.
- Code rejected → start a **new** `gcloud auth login --no-launch-browser` (codes are single-use).
- Firebase deploy fails → run `firebase login` with the same Google account.
